Z||000000||jeffndebrus||11-07-2001||07:53 PM||||my electric windows are re-a-l-l-y slow<BR>what to do  the car sat up for a year before I got it. Can I lubricate them and with what.||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroRacer||11-07-2001||08:05 PM||||It could just be a weak battery||||reg||1
Z||000002||jeffndebrus||11-07-2001||09:05 PM||||battery weak--could be<P>but I was driving it at the time<BR>shouldn't the alternator take over then??<P>Lubricate regulators with?????||||reg||1
Z||000003||webbee||11-07-2001||09:32 PM||||I spray all the channels and rubber, basically any place the glass contacts, with silicone spray. Then run the window up and down while it's still wet. This works the silicone around.  After it dries you will have to clean the over spray off the glass and plastic. Works great for freeing up any windows.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||11-08-2001||08:40 AM||||Or use silicon grease to avoid the mess.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||11-08-2001||08:22 PM||||I thought I had this in my cave but that update never got posted. Should be there in the next few days...<P>Don't spray anything all over the place. Don't lube the nose or tail tracks with the plastic linings. Depending on what you get in them you could damage the liners and make them bind worse later.<P>You are after the metal lift and guide tracks that the rollers run in. The light track is attached to the glass. The guide track runs vertical behind where the arm rest goes.<P>Bend/extend the little tube that comes with some spray oil and get oil into the rollers in the lift and guide tracks.<P>Grease the tracks with White or Silicone grease. These don't stink when they get hot like some others do.<P>Get some grease on the lift teeth.<P>shoot the counter spring with some oil or spread the coils with a screw driver and grease them. (Grease is better.)<P>For spray oil I like CRC 556, Valvoline's Synpower, or Valvoline's pyroil spray white grease. These cary more lube than WD40 and most other penetrating oils.WD 40 mostly evaporates and Liquid Wrench's formula can freeze in cold weather. (Learned that after using Liquid Wrench in a door lock...)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Spyder||11-09-2001||10:01 PM||||I used the white marine grade bearing grease on the teeth, rollers, and in the metal rails and all the pivot points. I made sure not to get the grease on anything that would get on the glass itself, so no greasy window.  <BR>Works great and smooth.  <BR>This make for a good time to check to make sure it is all lined up.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||11-10-2001||05:00 AM||||I use white waterproof lithium grease in a spray can and long tube nozzle. it dont get everywhere like that.||||reg||1
